{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}],"title":"Concurrent Order Selection with AutoARIMA"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaparallel"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMACriterion"],"title":"Automated Time Series","anchor":"Automated-Time-Series"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAParallel"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Discover optimal autoregressive, integrated, and moving average orders across ((p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s) grids using parallel Swift Concurrency.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Manually diagnosing autocorrelation functions (ACF) and partial autocorrelation functions (PACF) to select ARIMA orders is time-consuming and error-prone. Standard automated packages like R’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"forecast::auto.arima","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or Python’s "},{"code":"pmdarima","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" search across candidate orders sequentially."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoARIMA"},{"type":"text","text":" evaluates the entire hyperparameter lattice simultaneously across all CPU cores on Apple Silicon using structured Swift Concurrency ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withThrowingTaskGroup"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Grid-Search-Architecture","type":"heading","text":"Grid Search Architecture"},{"code":["           Observed Time Series [y_1, y_2, ..., y_N]","                               │","       ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐","       ▼                       ▼                       ▼","ARIMA(1, 1, 0)          ARIMA(2, 1, 1)          ARIMA(0, 1, 2)","Task 1                  Task 2                  Task 3","   │                       │                       │","   ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen","   └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC","       │                       │                       │","       └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘","                               ▼","                withThrowingTaskGroup Collector","                               │","                               ▼","                 Sorted Leaderboard & Best Model"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"text":"Information Criteria","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Information-Criteria"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"AIC (Akaike Information Criterion)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Penalizes model complexity while rewarding likelihood:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"$$\\text{AIC} = 2k - 2\\ln(L)$$"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"BIC (Bayesian Information Criterion)","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Imposes a stronger penalty proportional to sample size:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"$$\\text{BIC} = k\\ln(N) - 2\\ln(L)$$"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example Usage","anchor":"Example-Usage"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Initialize AutoARIMA with bounded search ranges","let autoArima = AutoARIMA(","    maxP: 3,","    maxD: 2,","    maxQ: 3,","    criterion: .aic",")","","\/\/ 2. Concurrently fit candidates across all cores","let result = try await autoArima.fit(series: historicalPrices)","print(\"Optimal Order: \\(autoArima.bestOrder!) with AIC: \\(autoArima.bestScore!)\")","","\/\/ 3. Generate multi-step forecasts","let forecast = try await autoArima.forecast(horizon: 12)","print(\"Forecasted points: \\(forecast.forecast.predictions)\")"]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMAOrder":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaorder","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"AutoARIMAOrder","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A structure identifying the selected ARIMA \/ SARIMA order."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMACriterion":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AutoARIMACriterion","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimacriterion","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AutoARIMACriterion","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"AutoARIMACriterion","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Information criterion utilized for model selection in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoARIMA"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMACriterion","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentat